BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Islington Village Planning Framework
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T210000
UID:1044@haveyoursay.toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Project: Planning Study Community Consultation Meetings\n\nThe
  City of Toronto’s Development Review Division\, in consultation with ot
 her City Divisions\, the community\, and local Councillors\, are beginning
  a Planning Framework process for the Islington Village area. This Plannin
 g Framework will review the existing policies\, strategies and guidelines 
 applicable to Islington Village to identify opportunities to reinforce the
  area’s main street village character. This work is in response to 2024 
 Council direction to conduct a scoped review of this area. The Islington V
 illage Planning Framework will focus on streetscape and public realm impro
 vements that enhance this character while addressing new Provincial policy
  changes. This meeting will be the first Community Consultation as part of
  this Planning Framework process.\n\nType: In person
LOCATION:Montgomery's Inn (Community Room)\, 4709 Dundas Street West\, Eto
 bicoke\, Toronto\, ON M9A 1A8\, Canada
URL:https://haveyoursay.toronto.ca/development-review-city-planning-planni
 ng-study-events/islington-village-planning-framework
X-SOURCE:City Planning Consultations
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North York at the Centre Public Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T200000
UID:1007@haveyoursay.toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Project: Planning Study Community Consultation Meetings\n\nOn 
 March 26\, 2026\, City Council endorsed the Recommended Option for managin
 g growth and change in North York Centre over the next 30 years. As part o
 f its decision\, Council directed staff to consider changes to the propose
 d parks network\, and proposed land uses and building types along Empress 
 Avenue\, Willowdale Avenue and in two blocks located northeast of Yonge St
 reet and Finch Avenue (PH28.6 Recommendation 13). Visit toronto.ca/nycentr
 e to learn more. Meeting materials will be posted when available.\n\nType:
  In person
LOCATION:100 Princess Ave\, North York\, Toronto\, ON M2N 3R7\, Canada
URL:https://haveyoursay.toronto.ca/development-review-city-planning-planni
 ng-study-events/north-york-centre-public-meeting
X-SOURCE:City Planning Consultations
END:VEVENT
